# The game is a shell that loads plain <script> files, and the C# port lives beside it. Both
# must never be ignored, and neither must ever have its line endings rewritten: every file here is
# LF-only by design, and a CRLF pass would break the byte-level encoding the middle-dot canary
# depends on. core.autocrlf is off in this repo for the same reason.
*
!.gitignore
!CONVENTIONS.md
!depths.html
!src/
src/*
!src/*.js

# the C# port. Source is tracked, build output is not.
!csharp/
csharp/*
!csharp/*.sln
csharp/Depths.Core/
!csharp/Depths.Core/
csharp/Depths.Core/*
!csharp/Depths.Core/*.cs
!csharp/Depths.Core/*.csproj
csharp/Depths.Tests/
!csharp/Depths.Tests/
csharp/Depths.Tests/*
!csharp/Depths.Tests/*.cs
!csharp/Depths.Tests/*.csproj

bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/
.idea/
!verify.ps1

# Session reports. The whitelist is by exception, so a new doc needs naming here or it is invisible
# to git - which is exactly what happened to REPORT.md, written and then silently not committed.
!REPORT.md

# The port manifest. Untracked until 2026-10-03, by the same mechanism one line above: it was written
# before the whitelist rule existed and nothing ever added it, so the file that exists to keep the
# C# port honest was itself not under version control. It is the most load-bearing document in the
# repo after CONVENTIONS.md and it was invisible to `git status` for its entire life.
!PORTED.md

# Scratch state for a session in progress. The start timestamp is written here at the beginning of
# a working session so that a report can state how long it took WITHOUT relying on remembering to
# note the time - an unattended session that ends in a power cut otherwise has no start time at all,
# which is exactly how the last one came to report 2h36m of commits as if it were a duration.
# Untracked on purpose: it is per-machine, per-session, and worthless to anyone else.
.session-start
